                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Nifty little game.  Not many stages, and kinda easy for me, but I've played alot of tank games. [Edit: There is a Score Grade, though, if you want to try for A+]\n\n 'Motion' wind indicator's a bit heavy, but essential to let the player know where they're moving (if any devs are reading this, please make 'thinner' wind :)  ).  Still a lot of fun though.  More arcadey than sim motion (you can't reverse 'and' turn at the same time, but you can go forward and turn, no problem). Love the aiming mechanic (Head-tracking)  Not sure how it will affect people with motion sickness, there's no teleporting, but it's very smooth when you move.\n\nA 'lot' more units, both enemy and even friendly units (It's only you, at the moment), wouldn't go astray.  This could develop into something very fun for strategy fans... if the devs, want it to.  At the moment, good for kids, VR noobs, and video game noobs in general.  Don't get me wrong, though, I had a blast, and wanted more :)",
